quran[30]{c,v,t}:
  78,1,What are they asking one another about?
  78,2,"(Is it) about the Great News,"
  78,3,regarding which they disagree?
  78,4,"No, indeed! They will soon come to know."
  78,5,"Again, no, indeed! They will soon come to know."
  78,6,"Did We not make the earth a resting place,"
  78,7,"and (fixed therein) the mountains like metal stakes,"
  78,8,"and create you in pairs,"
  78,9,"and make your sleep a repose,"
  78,10,"and make the night a covering,"
  78,11,"and make the day for livelihood,"
  78,12,"and build the seven mighty heavens above you,"
  78,13,"and place (the sun as) a radiant lamp (i.e. a source of heat and light),"
  78,14,"and send down pouring water from the rain clouds,"
  78,15,"so that We may produce by it grains and vegetation,"
  78,16,and dense (and) luxuriant gardens?
  78,17,"Indeed, the Day of Judgement is an appointed moment."
  78,18,"(That is) the Day when the Trumpet will be blown, and you all will come out in crowds,"
  78,19,"and the heavens will be opened and become (like) gates,"
  78,20,and the mountains (after being reduced to dust) will be blown away and become a mirage.
  78,21,"Indeed, Hell is (lying) in ambush,"
  78,22,"a place of return for the rebellious,"
  78,23,to reside there for endless ages.
  78,24,"They will not taste therein any coolness nor drink,"
  78,25,"except boiling water and pus (oozing from the wounds of the inmates of Hell),"
  78,26,as a fitting recompense (for their rebellion).
  78,27,"Indeed, they were not anticipating any Reckoning."
  78,28,They denied Our signs with utter rejection.
  78,29,And We have everything recorded precisely in a Book.
  78,30,So taste! We shall increase you in nothing but punishment.
